The PR makes workspace imports idempotent, canonicalizes filesystem identity without collapsing distinct case-sensitive directories, adds database-level exact-path uniqueness, and emits sidebar folder snapshots before Git-origin discovery completes.
- Consolidates legacy exact-path duplicates while preserving related project data and selection.
- Serializes same-service registration and uses SQLite conflict handling across service instances.
- Resolves Git origins asynchronously with bounded lookup time.

<h3>Confidence Score: 4/5</h3>

The PR should not merge until workspace removal is serialized with the new idempotent existing-project return path.

A concurrent re-import and removal can make workspace.add successfully return a project row that workspace.remove has already deleted.

**Files Needing Attention:** apps/server/src/workspace/layers/workspace-service.ts

<details><summary><h3>Important Files Changed</h3></summary>




| Filename | Overview |
|----------|----------|
| apps/server/src/workspace/layers/workspace-service.ts | Adds canonical-path idempotency and registration serialization, but removal can race the new existing-row return path. |
| apps/server/src/persistence/migrations/0052_unique_project_paths.ts | Consolidates exact duplicate projects, transfers known references, and adds a unique path index. |
| apps/renderer/src/lib/environment-shell-client-bus.ts | Emits workspace folders immediately and fills missing Git origins asynchronously. |
| packages/git/src/git-service-live.ts | Bounds origin discovery to five seconds and normalizes expected repository failures to no origin. |

</details>


<details><summary><h3>Sequence Diagram</h3></summary>

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
  participant A as workspace.add
  participant DB as SQLite
  participant R as workspace.remove
  A->>DB: Find existing project
  DB-->>A: Existing folder row
  R->>DB: Delete same project
  DB-->>R: Removed
  A-->>A: Return now-stale Folder
```
</details>


